  "notes": "## Intuition\n\nA path exists exactly when `destination` belongs to the same connected piece of the graph as `source`. So start at `source` and explore: from every vertex reached, step along all its edges to vertices not visited yet. If the search ever pops `destination`, a path exists; if it runs out of vertices first, none does. A simpler but slower idea is to sweep the edge list again and again, spreading \"reached\" across any edge with one reached end, until nothing changes; that can take O(n · E).\n\n## Approach\n\n1. Build `graph`, an adjacency list, adding each edge in both directions.\n2. Mark `source` in `seen` and push it onto `stack`.\n3. Pop a `node`. If it is `destination`, return `true`.\n4. Push every unvisited neighbour `next`, marking it as `seen` when it is pushed so it enters the stack only once.\n5. When the stack is empty, every reachable vertex was visited without meeting `destination`: return `false`.\n\n## Example 1, step by step\n\n`n = 3`, `edges = [[0,1],[1,2],[2,0]]`, `source = 0`, `destination = 2`.\n\n- `graph` is `0: [1,2]`, `1: [0,2]`, `2: [1,0]`.\n- `stack = [0]`, `seen = [true,false,false]`.\n- Pop 0: not the destination. Push 1 and 2; `stack = [1,2]`.\n- Pop 2: it is the destination, so return `true`.\n\n## Complexity\n\n- Time: O(n + E): each vertex is pushed at most once and each edge is looked at twice.\n- Space: O(n + E) for the adjacency list, `seen` and the stack.\n\n## Pitfalls\n\n- Edges work both ways; adding only `u -> v` misses paths like `2 -> 0` stored as `[0,2]`.\n- Mark a vertex when it is pushed, not when it is popped, or a dense graph pushes it many times.\n- When `source === destination` the answer is `true` even with no edges.\n- A recursive DFS can overflow the call stack on a long chain of vertices; an explicit stack avoids that.\n\n## Variables\n\n| Name | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `graph` | adjacency list: the neighbours of each vertex |\n| `u`, `v` | the two ends of an edge |\n| `seen` | whether a vertex has already been pushed |\n| `stack` | vertices waiting to be explored |\n| `node` | the vertex being explored |\n| `next` | a neighbour of `node` |",
  "narration": {
    "2": "Make an empty neighbour list for every vertex.",
    "3": "Go through the edges once to fill the lists.",
    "4": "Record that v can be reached from u...",
    "5": "...and that u can be reached from v, because edges work both ways.",
    "7": "No vertex has been visited yet.",
    "8": "The search starts from source.",
    "9": "Mark source so it is never pushed again.",
    "10": "Keep exploring while some reached vertex is still waiting.",
    "11": "Take the most recently found vertex: this is what makes the search depth-first.",
    "12": "Did the search reach the destination?",
    "13": "Yes: a path from source exists.",
    "15": "Look at every neighbour of this vertex.",
    "16": "Skip neighbours that are already on the stack or done.",
    "17": "Mark it now so it is pushed only once.",
    "18": "Push it so it is explored later.",
    "22": "Everything reachable from source was explored without meeting destination."
  }
}
